window.EN={"1":"Having defeated Alcardo, Etruria's former governor-general of the Three Western Isles,","2":"Roy and his army finally advance their forces into the great plains of Sacae.","3":"But ever since Bern's invasion, Sacae—","4":"the tribes that defied Bern and the Djute tribe who follow them had been almost entirely wiped out,","5":"and the chieftain of the Kutolah tribe, defeated by Bern, who is said to be the greatest warrior even in Sacae—","6":"the \"Grey Wolf\" Dayan and his men, though continuing a guerrilla resistance,","7":"could be said to have become, for the most part, a pro-Bern power.","8":"Just as Roy's group reached the middle of the great plains,","9":"the Djute tribe, now the largest tribe on the plains, using tactics unique to the plains,","10":"blocks the path ahead of Roy's group.","11":"An Etrurian army has appeared to the west!","12":"Hm. As planned, lure them into our camp.","13":"Let's make them learn just how terrifying we are.","14":"Did you send word to the other tribes?","15":"Yes.","16":"There is deep resentment toward our Djute tribe for being close with Bern, but—","17":"—quite a few are rushing to help, saying we must stand against Etruria's invasion.","18":"I see... Compared to our battle with that \"Grey Wolf,\" this one's much easier.","19":"After all, the enemy is an \"invading\" army.","20":"Against those who come to invade, we unite and fight...","21":"Right. That's the Law of Sacae.","22":"Our fight with the \"Grey Wolf\" Dayan's Kutolah tribe was seen as a fight between tribes,","23":"so no one else got involved.","24":"But in truth, we had the backing of Bern's army...","25":"That's how it is.","26":"Although, as a result, there are quite a few who resent the fact","27":"that Bern now secretly controls Sacae.","28":"That's true. Right now, there are quite a few tribes and forces","29":"who sympathize with and are sheltering the \"Grey Wolf\" Dayan, who fights us and Bern like a guerrilla.","30":"Since his tribe was destroyed too, he should just obediently follow us.","31":"It's not as though he doesn't know the fate of those who fought Bern head-on.","32":"The great city of Bulgar, for instance, defied Bern, and was attacked and completely conquered.","33":"From here on, those who, like our Djute tribe, skillfully maneuver among the strong will win.","34":"For that, I'll make the most of that old-fashioned \"Law of Sacae.\"","35":"Princess Guinivere...","36":"From here on, our army will be drawing closer to Bern.","37":"...Yes.","38":"Accordingly, the chances of fighting Bern's soldiers are increasing too.","39":"Eventually, it will come to a full-scale battle with the army of the Kingdom of Bern.","40":"......","41":"Before that, there's something I'd like to ask you, Princess.","42":"What is it?","43":"It's something I heard from someone the other day, but—","44":"—that King Zephiel killed the former king of Bern... his own father... and took the throne that way...","45":"!!","46":"I couldn't believe that story was true.","47":"Because, think about it!","48":"Princess Guinivere, you were prepared to even abandon your own country","49":"in order to try to stop it.","50":"If King Zephiel really were the cruel man the story makes him out to be,","51":"you wouldn't have thought to go that far, would you, Princess?","52":"......","53":"The reason I","54":"took the Fire Emblem into my keeping from you","55":"wasn't just to fight Bern,","56":"but because I thought I might be able to search, to the very end, for the \"path to peace\" you wished for.","57":"Lord Roy...","58":"So please, won't you let me hear the truth from your own lips, Princess?","59":"I'm sorry... please... just give me a little more time.","60":"! Princess Guinivere!!","61":"As long as there's an enemy within our camp, every tribe keeps up the attack...","62":"That's the Law of Sacae.","63":"Each tribe sets up camp surrounding the castle and meets any intruder head-on...","64":"That's the Law of Sacae.","65":"Against invaders, all the tribes unite and stand against them...","66":"That's the Law of Sacae.","67":"Every day without fail, we offer prayers to the earth and the stars...","68":"That's the Law of Sacae.","69":"That's it... just like that, come closer.","70":"We'll dye our camp through with your blood.","71":"※If attacked with Sue: You... the granddaughter of Dayan of the Kutolah tribe...","72":"......","73":"※If attacked with Sin: ...A survivor of the Kutolah tribe?","74":"Monke! Know the grudge of my tribe!","75":"Gah... ha... I... misjudged...","76":"I never thought... it would come to this...","77":"Quite the tough opponent, that was.","78":"But with this, we should have struck down Sacae's greatest enemy.","79":"Though the remaining forces are still a concern...","80":"It seems they're gathering together, waiting for a chance to counterattack.","81":"Do you know where they're trying to gather?","82":"I've sent out scouts — they should be back by now, I'd think.","83":"I'll go take a look.","84":"...Lord Roy.","85":"Princess Guinivere. What's the matter?","86":"Will you... will you hear me out... about my brother?","87":"!! ...Are you sure?","88":"Yes... after all, I want you to know, before we enter Bern.","89":"About the dreadful thing that happened within the royal family of Bern.","90":"...The other day, you asked whether my brother — King Zephiel of Bern—","91":"—had killed our father, the former king, didn't you?","92":"Yes...","93":"To give you the conclusion first... it is true.","94":"! Then it's really true — King Zephiel, aiming for the throne, killed his own father...?","95":"That part is wrong!","96":"Wrong? Didn't he assassinate the former king for the sake of the throne?","97":"That's not it... It was my father... who tried to assassinate first.","98":"Eh! Th-then King Zephiel...","99":"Unable to bear his tyrannical conduct any longer, he... killed our father... with his own hands...","100":"What on earth...","101":"...Lord Roy. We've found where the enemy army is gathering!","102":"Hm? What's the matter, you two?","103":"No... um... some other time...","104":"...Could it be that my coming here just now was bad timing?","105":"No, that's not it. Anyway, where's the enemy army gathering?","106":"Yes, a city called Bulgar.","107":"Bulgar... I've heard of that.","108":"It was originally the greatest city in all of Sacae, after all.","109":"Though it was attacked by Bern once and crushed...","110":"I see... Understood. Let's head there right away.","111":"But why would Bern's former king... his own son...?"};
